/* Ad032 - Schema-EXPRESS rule recursion bomb
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   Catalog section : §12.11 adversarial (sub-class: resource-exhaustion / DoS)
   Sources         : 12-adversarial.md A032
   See also        : Ad027, Ad054, Ad055, Pf030
   Severity        : M (DoS)
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   WARNING: This file is INTENTIONALLY MALFORMED for parser-robustness
   testing. Do NOT use as exchange data.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   Defect
     EXPRESS WHERE rules invoke functions transitively. An attacker
     references entities such that rule evaluation walks the entity
     graph repeatedly. With a star topology, an O(n^2) evaluation with
     cycle re-entry is weaponisable: rule re-checks fan out across every
     EDGE_CURVE -> VERTEX_POINT pair, then back-link.
   Reproducer recipe (scaled-down 16-edge star here; production size 10^4)
     Sixteen EDGE_CURVE entities each referencing the same two
     VERTEX_POINTs in a star topology. WHERE rules on edge curves and
     vertices repeatedly traverse this set on every binding.
   Expected kernel behavior
     Per-file rule-evaluation budget; abort with E_RULE_BUDGET when
     budget exceeded. Memoise WHERE-rule results per entity; never
     re-evaluate beyond a bounded depth.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------
*/
